-- title:
--   K-finite cusp functions with classes in a closed cuspidal subrepresentation
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, $\alpha,\beta$ real numbers and $\Phi_0$ a set of adelic $2\times 2$ invertible matrices over $F$ which is a slab fundamental domain, i.e. $0<\alpha<\beta$, $\Phi_0$ lies in the slab where the determinant norm is between $\alpha$ and $\beta$, and $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the action of the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ on the adelic Haar measure restricted to that slab. Let $\sigma$ be real, let $\xi$ be a homomorphism from the full subgroup of idele units of $F$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ whose modulus is $\sigma$, in the sense that $\|\xi(z)\|$ equals the $\sigma$-th power of the idele norm of $z$ for every $z$, and let $M$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of the cuspidal subcarrier $\mathrm{cuspSubcarrier}$ (the topological closure, inside the carrier attached to $\Phi_0$ and $\sigma$, of the image of the continuous smooth cuspidal members) which satisfies `IsClosedCuspSubrep`: $M$ is closed, and $M$ is carried into itself by every continuous linear endomorphism of the cuspidal subcarrier which is a cusp lift of right translation by an element of the finite adelic $\mathrm{GL}_2$ subgroup, of right translation by $\mathrm{rowIsometryInclAt}_0$ of an element of the row-isometry subgroup at an infinite place, or of right convolution by a factorizable test function that is archimedean bi-finite for some archimedean type family. The conclusion is that the submodule of functions on adelic $\mathrm{GL}_2$ obtained by intersecting the $K$-finite cuspidal submodule $\mathrm{cuspKFiniteSubmodule}$ at the pins $\mathrm{fdPins}\,F\,\Phi_0$ (Borel structure and adelic Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2$, domain $\Phi_0$, full central subgroup, level-one subgroups intersected with the finite subgroup, Hecke generators, and the adelic additive Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box) with the image, under the inclusion of the submodule of continuous smooth cuspidal members, of the preimage of $M$ under the class map $\mathrm{toCuspSubcarrier}$, is a cuspidal subrepresentation at those pins: it is contained in the $K$-finite cuspidal submodule and is stable under right translation by finite adelic elements, under right translation by archimedean row isometries, and under right convolution by factorizable archimedean bi-finite test functions.
--
--   This is the function-level counterpart of a closed invariant subspace of the cuspidal spectrum: it transports a closed cuspidal subrepresentation $M$ of the Hilbert-space subcarrier back to the space of $K$-finite cuspidal automorphic functions whose classes lie in $M$. It is used in the transfer of irreducibility, where the subrepresentation generated by a typed level cut is compared with such a pullback.
